Use existing Zod validation and trusted property definitions.

Reject:

- Arbitrary JavaScript.
- HTML event-handler injection.
- Unsafe URL schemes.
- Unrestricted CSS expressions.
- Invalid dimensions.
- Unsupported CSS property names.
- Non-finite numeric values.
- Malformed color values.
- Invalid shape values.

Do not use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for property rendering.

## 66. Protect business data

The inspector must never allow changing through visual properties:

- Product price.
- Currency.
- Affiliate URL.
- Product identity.
- Retailer destination.
- Inventory status.
- Category database identity.
- Administrator permissions.
- Private configuration.

These belong to their proper business-management interfaces.

## 67. Enforce authorization

Only authorized administrators may save design changes.

Client-side component locks are not security authorization.

Keep the existing Supabase RLS and trusted server validation protections active.

Do not expose service-role credentials in browser code.

